{
  "$comment": "Native inventory of the pipeline pack (M10 G1), read by tools/release/native-licences.mjs and notices.mjs. `libs`: every DLL, dylib, shared object and executable the pack ships that is not a Python distribution's own extension module, matched by path globs relative to the scanned folder (** is any number of folders, case is ignored). `ports`: every vcpkg port our native builds use (tools/pipeline-pack/native), checked against the SBOMs vcpkg writes; a new port or version fails the gate until this file says what it is. `forbiddenPorts` and `forbiddenFiles` (regular expressions on file names) fail the gate whatever the rows say. Licences are judged by licence-policy.mjs against licence-exceptions.json; `exception` names a `runtimes` entry there, and an LGPL row must be a shared library named in `lgplShared`.",
  "schema": "native-libs/1",
  "forbiddenPorts": [
    {
      "name": "suitesparse-cholmod",
      "why": "CHOLMOD: LGPL modules and the GPL Supernodal, MatrixOps and Modify modules"
    },
    {
      "name": "suitesparse-spqr",
      "why": "SPQR is GPL-2.0-or-later"
    },
    {
      "name": "suitesparse-umfpack",
      "why": "UMFPACK is GPL-2.0-or-later"
    },
    {
      "name": "suitesparse-ldl",
      "why": "LDL is LGPL-2.1-or-later and would be linked statically"
    },
    {
